# Hendo Academy Website Structure

## Overview
The Hendo Academy website is a Next.js App Router site (`output: 'export'`) hosted on GitHub Pages. It promotes the study of Syriac and the history of Nasranies of India.

## Main routes
- [`app/page.tsx`](mdc:app/page.tsx) — Home (`/`) with About, Activities, Articles, Books, Editor, Videos, Contact
- [`app/articles/page.tsx`](mdc:app/articles/page.tsx) — Articles index (`/articles/`)
- [`app/editor/page.tsx`](mdc:app/editor/page.tsx) — Syriac Editor iframe (`/editor/`)
- [`app/books/*/page.tsx`](mdc:app/books) — Book iframe pages

## Articles
Article pages live under `app/articles/<slug>/page.tsx`. Metadata for the index is in [`lib/articles.ts`](mdc:lib/articles.ts). Listed articles must also appear in [`public/sitemap.xml`](mdc:public/sitemap.xml). See the new-article-metadata and new-article-sitemap rules.

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui
- Brand colors: primary `#8a3c3c`, secondary `#d4a445`, tertiary `#3c5c8a`
- Karshon and East Syriac fonts under `/assets/fonts/`
- Use `.syriac` / `SyriacText` for Syriac text

## Technical notes
- Static export for GitHub Pages; deploy via `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`
- Never add `.html` to hrefs and other links — use extensionless Next.js paths (e.g. `/articles/turgama`)
- `trailingSlash: false` so GitHub Pages URLs match the legacy site
- Shared chrome: `SiteHeader`, `SiteFooter`, `Analytics`, `Utterances`
- Static assets live in `public/` and keep their public URL paths
